      "content": "verdigris, a green or greenish blue substance obtained artificially by the action of dilute acetic acid on thin plates of copper (or a green rust naturally forming on copper and brass), and much used as a pigment, in dyeing, the arts, and medicine (OED s.v. Spanish a. 7, verdigris; OED s.v. verdigris)"
